al elements are all present: 8 footnotes, `![图 2-11：Skills 渐进式披露机制](images/fig2-11.svg)`, matching headings, and code spans (`SKILL.md`, `/tmp/leaked.txt`, `<external_content source=\"webpage\">...</external_content>`) preserved. However bold spans are shifted versus the source: \"完整 schema 则**按需追加到上下文末尾**\" pulls \"on demand\" into the bold that the English limits to \"**appended to the end of the context**\"; and in the KV paragraph the em-dash parenthetical and footnote URLs are kept but the blockquote terminal `>` structure and the italicized book title are normalized (title changed to Chinese 《Skill 可视化指南》 instead of the source's English italic title)."}},"preferred":"X","preference_evidence":"X shows strictly higher fidelity with no measurable omissions: it preserves the source's quoted English strings (the Trump-style example, \"help with backend\", the Baoyu footnote and book title), keeps the proper noun \"ReAct\", keeps \"Agent Skills\" and \"Python's pip / Node.js's npm\" intact, and maintains consistent 提示词工程/提示注入 terminology; Y drops the Python/Node.js attribution, invents a Chinese book title, rewrites quoted examples, paraphrases ReAct as \"推理-行动\", and mixes 提示工程 with 提示词. X's only real fault (\"输入过滤\" for Input Sanitization) is a single term slip, whereas Y's issues span accuracy, terminology, and a shifted bold span in markdown. Both are fluent, so accuracy and terminology decide the outcome in X's favor."} } }

